  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "4f99aa05-cf20-4a87-b250-0d25fe8eb536",
    "name": "Job Portal API",
    "description": "## Job Portal API\n\nThis collection contains API tests for a **Job Portal** application, covering the full workflow from user authentication to job management and application tracking.\n\n### Overview\n\nThe Job Portal API is built around three core workflows:\n\n- **Authentication** — Register as a candidate or employer, and log in to receive authentication tokens used across all protected endpoints.\n    \n- **Jobs** — Employers can post new job listings, candidates can browse available jobs, and candidates can apply for positions.\n    \n- **Applications** — Candidates can view their submitted applications, employers can review applications for their job postings, and employers can update application statuses (e.g., accepted or rejected).\n    \n\n### Getting Started\n\n1. **Set up the environment** — The collection uses the `Job-Portal_environment` environment. Ensure `baseUrl` is set to your server address (e.g., `http://localhost:5000`).\n    \n2. **Register & Login** — Run the requests in the **Auth** folder to register users and obtain tokens. The `employerToken` and `candidateToken` environment variables are used to authenticate subsequent requests.\n    \n3. **Run the workflows** — Use the **Jobs** and **Applications** folders to test job posting, applying, and application management.\n    \n\n### Folders\n\n| Folder | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Auth** | User & employer registration, and login |\n| **Jobs** | Add jobs, apply for jobs, and retrieve job listings |\n| **Applications** | View and manage job applications |",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "59017632",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/59017632-4f99aa05-cf20-4a87-b250-0d25fe8eb536?source=collection_link"
  },
